# D-22 / D-24: `@ buf[0] + buf[1] + buf[2]` is an int pointer (L2 spec 18.2).
# Returning it as int is an incompatible type, not a silent pointer-as-int
# and not the old blanket "not yet supported". `@ buf[i]` alone (D-21) and
# the same arithmetic into `@: int` (unit_addr_own_array_arith) are unaffected.
fn: sum_address () int
    []: int buf 3
    buf[0]: 1
    buf[1]: 2
    buf[2]: 3
    return: @ buf[0] + buf[1] + buf[2]
end: sum_address
